Z||000000||Ozzy||06-17-2000||02:18 AM||||Hi fellow Fiero owners...<P>Have been on the road trying to get my Sh*t together again. Sittin' in a motel in Utah, with my wife 7.5 mths pregnant, with our cat...waiting for my new gig to start and looking for a house. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Anything interesting happen while I've been out? I see ogre is diverting his energies to a more important cause. I hope he gains a speedy recovery.<P>On another note, in justification of our lil' iron duke powered cars...(never thought I'd be saying this!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) I have dragged my coupe from Seattle, thru Idaho and down into Utah, then shot down to Vegas briefly (106 deg...ugh!)and back to Provo, UT. The car did not miss so much as a beat! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It ran a little warmer than I like it to but never overheated and in the middle of some serious dessert! Last problem I had was a rear hub assy. and nuthin' since. Got 37 mpg to boot. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The GT rode behind the Ryder truck and got smeared with diesel and 1000 miles o'road grime. Washed off o.k. though...<P>If I don't get some bucks coming in soon there will be 2 VERY cheap Fiero's on th Mall! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I have this new job almost for certain but it is taking FOREVER to tie it down.<P>Ozzy||||reg||14
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||06-17-2000||01:49 PM||||Hey there Ozzy. I have been MIA too. I have been in Driggs, Idaho building a cabin in the middle of B.F.E. Not much to do there, but the scenery is AWESOME. Every day I see a hawk circling the fields hunting... very impressive birds. And the Tetons are massive. I am back for the weekend and going back for atleast another week.<P>P.s. you have email coming later.||||reg||1
